<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />

    <!--
        Background playback. Both permissions are required from API 34 for a service of type
        `mediaPlayback`, and the type is required because Android 17's background-audio hardening applies to
        every app that interacts with audio while it has no visible activity - whether or not it targets API
        37. `targetSdk` here is 36, so the rule is live already.

        The hardening's failure mode is the reason this is worth a comment: playback is suppressed with no
        exception and no failure message from any API, so an app that is wrong about it looks like one whose
        audio works intermittently rather than like one that is misconfigured.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK" />

    <!--
        Required from API 33, and it is load-bearing rather than cosmetic: a `MediaSessionService` becomes a
        foreground service **by posting a media notification** — that notification *is* the foreground
        notification. So without this permission the app cannot hold a foreground claim at all, and on
        Android 17 the platform then silently refuses its background audio while logging only
        `AudioHardening background playback muted ... level: partial`.

        Measured rather than reasoned: before this declaration the service did not exist at all. See
        docs/decisions.md 23.21, and tools/probe-background-audio.ps1 which reports this permission's state
        alongside the service's.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS" />

    <application
        android:name=".ReaderApplication"
        android:allowBackup="true"
        android:label="Notion Reader"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.NotionReader">

        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true">

            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />

                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>

        </activity>

        <!--
            The media session host. `exported="true"` is required rather than incidental: the system's media
            controls and the lock screen are external clients and must be able to bind to it. The action
            filter is what makes it discoverable by them.

            `foregroundServiceType="mediaPlayback"` is what exempts the app from the background-audio
            restriction, and it is the type the hardening documentation names. Starting this service while the
            app is visible is what grants it while-in-use capability, which is why the service is started from
            a user-initiated playback command rather than lazily once the screen has gone off.
        -->
        <service
            android:name=".PlaybackService"
            android:exported="true"
            android:foregroundServiceType="mediaPlayback">

            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="androidx.media3.session.MediaSessionService" />
            </intent-filter>

        </service>

    </application>

</manifest>
